Native BS-RoFormer vocal separation for WanGP

Architecture: lucidrains/BS-RoFormer (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Phil Wang).
https://github.com/lucidrains/BS-RoFormer
LICENSE_BS_ROFORMER accompanies the code. Rotary positions follow
rotary-embedding-torch (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 Phil Wang).

Inference code and chunked separation: audio-separator 0.36.1
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 karaokenerds), separator/uvr_lib_v5/roformer and
separator/architectures/mdxc_separator.py.
https://github.com/nomadkaraoke/python-audio-separator
LICENSE_AUDIO_SEPARATOR accompanies the code.

Changes: inference only (training loss, linear attention and dropout removed),
the configuration of the one checkpoint WanGP uses fixed in model.py, separate
q/k/v projections through WanGP's attention kit and shared kernels, weights
managed by MMGP. audio-separator and ONNX Runtime are not used.

Weights: model_bs_roformer_ep_317_sdr_12.9755 (BS-RoFormer vocals model by
viperx, distributed with Ultimate Vocal Remover and audio-separator), repacked
as model_bs_roformer_ep_317_sdr_12.9755_bf16.safetensors: WanGP key names,
the fused q/k/v projection stored as three matrices, BF16 weights.
